open - open a note file

usage: open [-sxna@] <wildcard>

    -s  open only boards that have unread items
    -x  open unread notes in OPEN mode
    -n  nonstop
    -a  disable "skip if not updated"
    -@  show scan completed/aborted

    With just an argument it shows the INDEX. INDEX lists 20 at a time
    (newest number first). Space for older page, BS for newer page,
    = for latest, * for oldest. Open older notes by number. Unread scan
    is new or open -s. f searches title/body then opens by number.
    A marks "since a time" as unread, k shows the board sign.
    Basenotes and responses go up to 9999 each (4-digit display).
    In INDEX: w = basenote, l = unread, q = quit, Enter opens the current
    note, v redraws the list. In OPEN: w = response, digits = response
    number, i = INDEX.
